#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/uz-Cyrl.rc -- Uzbek (Cyrillic), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "uz-Cyrl"`.
//
// Stage E108, group A: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc. The second script of Uzbek (decision 200b.1): the words and the
// meaning are those of uz.rc, letter for letter in the Cyrillic of the language (the letters
// short u with breve, ka with descender, ghe with stroke, ha with descender are used); one
// glossary for both scripts, l10n/glossary/uz-Cyrl.tsv in the control contour. Keys stay in
// Latin letters as the hotkey field prints them (RULES 4); the quotation marks are « ».
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Uzbek (Cyrillic) — `[general] language = "uz-Cyrl"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
